        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0499697e-886d-5850-a9ee-f9a559c0c000",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Bands: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party\n- Publications: NME\n- Places: South London, Glasgow\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n- Albums: You Could Have It So Much Better\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people that is made without concern for imitation or presentation.\n- South London's Art Brut were named after Jean Dubuffet's definition of outsider art.\n- NME tagged South London's Art Brut as part of the Art Wave scene alongside bands such as The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band that formed in 2002 and are based in Glasgow.\n- You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by the Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
